  "question": {
    "text": "Identify the pair in which the geometry of the species is T-shaped and square-pyramidal, respectively,"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>ICl</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ICl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>IO</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi>IO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>.</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>IO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>.</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0204_93bc0153766f.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 333px;\" /><br /><br />In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, the central atom has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;bond pairs and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> lone pairs. Hence, the electrons will enter a trigonal bipyramidal geometry. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> lone pairs will take up equatorial positions giving the molecule a T-shape. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Xe</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> bond pairs and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> lone pair. The electrons will take up square bipyramidal geometry, but due to a lone pair, the shape of the molecule will be square pyramidal."
  }
}